```tsx
await addSupply(user, { name: "Cobalt blue", supplier: "Laguna", category: "glaze", quantity: "5" });
await addSupply(user, { name: "Cobalt blue", supplier: "Laguna", category: "glaze", quantity: "3" });
expect alert "You already track this item from this supplier"
await addSupply(user, { name: "Cobalt blue", supplier: "Amaco", category: "glaze", quantity: "3" });
expect(screen.getAllByText("Cobalt blue")).toHaveLength(2);
```

4. "Edit a supply"
```tsx
seedStorage(SUPPLY_STORAGE_KEY, [makeItem({ name: "Cobalt blue", quantity: 8 })]);
render(<App />);
await user.click(screen.getByRole("button", { name: "Edit Cobalt blue" }));
const dialog = screen.getByRole("dialog", { name: "Edit Cobalt blue" });
await user.clear(within(dialog).getByLabelText("Quantity left"));
await user.type(within(dialog).getByLabelText("Quantity left"), "3");
await user.click(within(dialog).getByRole("button", { name: "Save changes" }));
expect(screen.getByText("3")).toBeInTheDocument();
```
Note: "3" might appear elsewhere (stat "Running low" = 1…). After editing quantity to 3, the item is no longer low. Stat: Supplies tracked 1, Running low 0, Out of stock 0. The table shows "3". getByText("3") — the stat values are "1", "0", "0". So "3" is unique. OK.

Also test supplier edit: change supplier to "Amaco" and verify "from Amaco".

5. "Delete a supply"
```tsx
seedStorage(...[makeItem({name: "Cobalt blue"})]);
render; click "Delete Cobalt blue"; dialog "Delete supply"; click "Delete";
expect(screen.getByText("No supplies yet")).toBeInTheDocument();
```

6. "Filter by type"
```tsx
seedStorage(SUPPLY_STORAGE_KEY, [
  makeItem({ name: "Cobalt blue", category: "glaze" }),
  makeItem({ name: "Stoneware", supplier: "Laguna Clay", category: "clay" }),
  makeItem({ name: "Wire cutters", supplier: "Bench Tools", category: "tools" }),
]);
render;
await user.selectOptions(screen.getByLabelText("Filter by type"), "clay");
expect(screen.getByText("Stoneware")).toBeInTheDocument();
expect(screen.queryByText("Cobalt blue")).not.toBeInTheDocument();
```

7. "Adjust quantity with +/−"
```tsx
seedStorage(...[makeItem({ name: "Cobalt blue", quantity: 4 })]);
render;
await user.click(screen.getByRole("button", { name: "Use one Cobalt blue" }));
expect(screen.getByText("3")).toBeInTheDocument();
await user.click(screen.getByRole("button", { name: "Add one Cobalt blue" }));
expect(screen.getByText("4")).toBeInTheDocument();
```
Note: after "Use one", quantity 3 → not low (3 > 2). Good, no badge interference. But wait — the stat "Running low" is 0. "3" is unique. OK.

8. "Survives a reload"
```tsx
// create via UI, verify persisted
render(<App />);
await addSupply(user, { name: "Cobalt blue", supplier: "Laguna", category: "glaze", quantity: "12" });
const stored = readStorage<SupplyItem>(SUPPLY_STORAGE_KEY);
expect(stored?.records).toHaveLength(1);
// simulate reload: unmount and re-render
rerender? 
```
Better: use `seedStorage` then render fresh:
```tsx
seedStorage(SUPPLY_STORAGE_KEY, [makeItem({ name: "Cobalt blue", quantity: 12 })]);
render(<App />);
expect(screen.getByText("Cobalt blue")).toBeInTheDocument();
```
And the UI→storage check in test 1 (after adding, readStorage has 1 record). That covers persistence in both directions.

9. "Corrupted storage still renders the app"
```tsx
corruptStorage(SUPPLY_STORAGE_KEY, "{not json");
render(<App />);
expect(screen.getByRole("heading", { name: "Studio Supplies" })).toBeInTheDocument();
expect(screen.getByRole("alert")).toHaveTextContent("unreadable");
```
Notice tone="warning" — does Notice render role="alert"? In the ui tests, Notice tone="error" → getByRole("alert"). Probably all tones use role="alert" (or status). The test used tone="error" and found role alert. For warning it might be role="status". Risky. Let me check the Notice implementation at lines 177–197.

Also, partially corrupted: seed with one valid + one invalid record → "1 damaged entry was skipped" message, valid record still shows. That's a better test for "corrupted saved data degrades". I'll do both: full corruption (reset message) and partial (skip message + valid record shown).

Let me check the Notice markup.

